## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The title strategy of `POST /api/verification/verify` has a comment block (`:1432-1445`) that explains what the existence query hides. Its bullets were updated by the KS-1114 follow-up: a draft, a revoked, a deleted or an expired match answers the ordinary not-found (the SQL at `:1466` is `lower(btrim(d.status)) NOT IN ('draft', 'revoked', 'deleted', 'expired')`). The closing summary line, `:1445`, was not updated: it still reads "Absent, another tenant's, draft, revoked and the sentinel all answer ONE not-found body.", so a reader of the summary alone is told that a deleted or expired document is a hit. The fix is to name `deleted` and `expired` in that line. It is a comment; no behaviour changes.

## Where

- `:1443-1444` - (correct) the two comment lines ending `...so a naive lookup would` / `...the very field that was erased.` - stay, hunk context.
- `:1445` - must change: `        // Absent, another tenant's, draft, revoked and the sentinel all answer ONE not-found body.` becomes `        // Absent, another tenant's, draft, revoked, deleted, expired and the sentinel all answer ONE not-found body.`
- `:1446` - (correct) `        if (titleToFind && !documentId && !computedHash) {` - stays, hunk context.
- `:1440-1441` - (correct) the bullet lines that already name a deleted or an expired match - stay.
- The test is a NEW file; nothing else changes.

