## Cells and controls

- RED `RED KS-1623 the summary comment names deleted` and `RED KS-1623 the summary comment names expired` - at the tip the summary line holds neither word, so `expect(SUMMARY).toContain(...)` fails (by assertion, no throw at load); after the edit both are green.
- CONTROL `CONTROL the instrument reads the real route: one summary line and the status predicate exist` - green both ways: exactly one line matches the summary pattern and the `lower(btrim(d.status)) NOT IN (...)` predicate is found (without it the RED cells could pass or fail against nothing).
- CONTROL `CONTROL the query hides exactly draft, revoked, deleted and expired` - green both ways: the status list is read out of the SQL, so the comment is compared with the real hidden set.
- CONTROL `CONTROL the summary names absent, another tenant, draft, revoked and the sentinel` - green both ways: the edit keeps the old words.

